# ─── What NOT to pack into the .vsix ──────────────────────────────────────
# The extension imports ONLY Node built-ins + the vscode API (no third-party
# runtime deps), so the entire node_modules tree is dev/packaging tooling and
# must never ship. Everything below is excluded from `vsce package`.

# Dependency tree — 17+ MB of dev/transitive tooling (vsce, typescript, etc.)
node_modules/**

# TypeScript sources & build config — only the compiled out/*.js needs to ship
src/**
**/*.ts
!out/**/*.d.ts
tsconfig.json
.eslintrc*
.editorconfig

# Source maps — not needed at runtime, ~half of out/
**/*.map

# Compiled test files — they compile into out/ for local `node --test` runs
# but must never ship in the packaged extension.
out/**/*.test.js
out/**/*.test.d.ts

# Previously-built packages / nested vsix artifacts
**/*.vsix
out/*.vsix

# Local codebase index — generated per-workspace, must never ship in the .vsix
.nexus/**

# Editor / VCS / CI noise
.vscode/**
.vscode-test/**
.github/**
.git/**
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Misc dev files
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
**/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
